\section{Discussion}
The hybrid compute fabric demonstrates that heterogeneous architectures can
achieve deterministic relativistic tensor evolution when synchronized through
femtosecond-scale optical coherence. The integration of quantum-timed
electronics provides a novel pathway for eliminating drift across large-scale
simulation pipelines. Wafer-scale PDE sweeps significantly enhance curvature
resolution, while GPU tensor cores maintain fine-grained evolution fidelity.

The results indicate that SASA-v9.0 is suitable for next-generation
astrophysical modeling, including gravitational-wave precursor analysis,
high-energy cosmological dynamics, and multi-instrument data fusion.